# Backend file naming

Do not name a layer file after the domain only (`auth.py`). The filename must include the layer.

Pattern: `{domain}_{layer}.py`

| Layer folder | Filename |
|---|---|
| `controller/` | `auth_controller.py` |
| `services/` | `auth_service.py` |
| `routes/` | `auth_routes.py` |
| `schema/` | `auth_schema.py` (when adding/renaming) |
| `middleware/` | `auth_middleware.py` (when adding/renaming) |

Examples:

```text
services/auth/controller/auth_controller.py   ✅
services/auth/services/auth_service.py        ✅
services/auth/routes/auth_routes.py           ✅

services/auth/controller/auth.py              ❌
services/food/routes/food.py                  ❌
```

The same rule applies to every future service (`food`, `nutrition`, etc.): `food_controller.py`, `food_service.py`, `food_routes.py`.
